{"name":"Brazen","hex":"#a87f12","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brazen","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of brass.","Brass-like in appearance or character; bright, ruddy, hard."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To turn a brass color.","Generally followed by out or through: to carry through in a brazen manner; to act boldly despite embarrassment, risk, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brazen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brass","blocks":[{"text":"Brass is an alloy of copper and zinc, in proportions which can be varied to achieve different colours and mechanical, electrical, acoustic, and chemical properties, but copper typically has the larger proportion, generally 2⁄3 copper and 1⁄3 zinc. In use since prehistoric times, it is a substitutional alloy: atoms of the two constituents may replace each other within the same crystal structure."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Planispheric_Astrolabe_MET_DP105325.jpg/330px-Planispheric_Astrolabe_MET_DP105325.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brass","wikidata":"Q39782"},{"title":"HMS Brazen","blocks":[{"text":"There have been a number of Royal Navy ships called HMS Brazen"},{"items":["HMS Brazen (1781) was a cutter purchased in 1781 and sold on 9 April 1799 for £340.","HMS Brazen (1798) was the French privateer L'Invincible General Bonaparte, taken in 1798; Brazen was wrecked in January 1800 near Newhaven.","HMS Brazen (1808) was a sixth-rate 28-gun sloop, launched in 1808 and broken up in 1848.","HMS Brazen (1856) was an Albacore-class gunboat","HMS Brazen (1896) was the lead ship of the Brazen-class destroyers, a C-class destroyer built at the end of the 19th century.","HMS Brazen (H80) was a B-class destroyer, built in 1930 and sunk by an air attack in 1940.","HMS Brazen (F91) was a Type 22 frigate sold to the Brazilian Navy in 1994, which renamed her Bosisio. She was expended as a target in 2017."]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HMS_Brazen","wikidata":"Q930397"},{"title":"Brazen (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Brazen is a 2022 American thriller film directed by Monika Mitchell. It is based on Nora Roberts' 1988 novel Brazen Virtue. The film stars Alyssa Milano, Sam Page, and Matthew Finlan."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c6/Brazen_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brazen_(film)","wikidata":"Q110303737"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Brass_lectern_in_the_form_of_an_eagle_attributed_to_Aert_van_Tricht_the_Elder%2C_Limburg_%28Netherlands%29%2C_c._1500%2C_The_Cloisters.jpg/500px-Brass_lectern_in_the_form_of_an_eagle_attributed_to_Aert_van_Tricht_the_Elder%2C_Limburg_%28Netherlands%29%2C_c._1500%2C_The_Cloisters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Brass_lectern_in_the_form_of_an_eagle_attributed_to_Aert_van_Tricht_the_Elder%2C_Limburg_%28Netherlands%29%2C_c._1500%2C_The_Cloisters.jpg/500px-Brass_lectern_in_the_form_of_an_eagle_attributed_to_Aert_van_Tricht_the_Elder%2C_Limburg_%28Netherlands%29%2C_c._1500%2C_The_Cloisters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Brass lectern with an eagle, attributed to Aert van Tricht, Limburg (Netherlands), circa 1500","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrass_lectern_in_the_form_of_an_eagle_attributed_to_Aert_van_Tricht_the_Elder%2C_Limburg_(Netherlands)%2C_c._1500%2C_The_Cloisters.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Microstructure_of_rolled_and_annealed_brass%3B_magnification_400X.jpg/500px-Microstructure_of_rolled_and_annealed_brass%3B_magnification_400X.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_cont